    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hm, okay. but if we look at the actual planning data, wouldn't it be more accurate to say that these 'identity' concerns are usually just code for NIMBYism? most experts seem to agree that density is essential for housing affordability and sustainability, so isn't it kind of a stretch to treat local opposition as having the same weight as those macro-level benefits?",
