      "content": "While the macro benefits of density are well-documented, dismissing local opposition as mere \"NIMBYism\" often ignores the complex, documented feedback loops where increased density disproportionately impacts low-to-moderate income residents without providing adequate affordable alternatives. Experts generally recognize that while large-scale housing is necessary, successful implementation relies heavily on navigating these specific local friction points to ensure equitable outcomes; treating them lightly can inadvertently spray the community with resistance. Therefore, acknowledging the weight of these concerns alongside macro data creates a more credible narrative that respects both policy goals and community realities.",
